{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "19", "m": "10", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "09", "M": "23", "S": "02"}}, "news": [{"title": "Panchkula: 18-acre illegal colony razed in Golpura", "para": "On Sunday, a significant demolition operation unfolded in Golpura village as the district town planning department removed unauthorized structures in an illegal colony covering 18 acres. Under the leadership of DTP Babita Gupta, the operation was fortified by a strong police presence for safety. Officials reiterated that developing colonies requires prior approval and warned of ongoing enforcement against illegal construction throughout the district to address unauthorized colonization.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/panchkula-18-acre-illegal-colony-razed-in-golpura/135038853?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-312390/135038853.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Farmers give consent, New Noida land acquisition set to begin soon", "para": "The Noida Authority is preparing to initiate land acquisition for New Noida, with 281 farmers already consenting to part with their plots. Finalized acquisition rates for the ambitious Dadri-Noida-Ghaziabad Investment Region, covering more than 20,000 hectares, are now in place. Planned in four phases, the aim is to secure 3,165 hectares by 2027.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/farmers-give-consent-new-noida-land-acquisition-set-to-begin-soon/135038829?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-254964/135038829.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Over 110 families in Kot Sekhon get property cards under \u2018Mera Ghar, Mere Naam\u2019 Scheme", "para": "Punjab cabinet minister Tarunpreet Singh Sond recently handed out property cards to 115 beneficiaries in Kot Sekhon village. This initiative aims to legally empower families who previously lacked clear ownership documentation. Utilizing surveys and digital mapping, these records will facilitate smoother access to bank loans and enhance future property transactions for generations to come.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/over-110-families-in-kot-sekhon-get-property-cards-under-mera-ghar-mere-naam-scheme/135038752?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-347504/135038752.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}]}